  bx('bl', '<b>14 + 1 + 3 + 4 = 22.</b> Order: Sindhi, the “KMN” trio, the “BDMS” four. Uses: representation in Official Language Commission; enriching Hindi; use in competitive exams. <b>96th Am (2011)</b>: “Oriya” became “Odia”.'),
  mn('K-M-N-B-D-M-S', '<b>After 1967:</b> <b>K</b>ind <b>M</b>others <b>N</b>urture <b>B</b>rave <b>D</b>aughters, <b>M</b>ighty <b>S</b>ons. K Konkani, M Manipuri, N Nepali (71st, 1992) · B Bodo, D Dogri, M Maithili, S Santhali (92nd, 2003). Sindhi (1967) came before.'),
  mn('S-K-M-N-B-D-M-S', '<b>S</b>indhi (1967), <b>K</b>onkani, <b>M</b>anipuri, <b>N</b>epali (1992), <b>B</b>odo, <b>D</b>ogri, <b>M</b>aithili, <b>S</b>anthali (2003): “<b>S</b>ix <b>K</b>ind <b>M</b>en <b>N</b>ever <b>B</b>ring <b>D</b>ull <b>M</b>aps, <b>S</b>ir.”'),
