  bx('ye', '<b>Source conflicts:</b> (1) Dates: handout ties the 1963 extension to protests in Tamil Nadu; the Act section puts violent protests in <b>1965</b> and veto in <b>1967</b>. Use: Act 1963, protests 1965, amendment 1967. (2) <b>Lakshmikanth</b> says the 1967 amendment made English compulsory for listed papers; handout puts it under <b>Section 3(3)</b>. Use handout. (3) LK says the Committee was due after ten years (came 1976); handout cites Section 4 with no date.'),
  sec('SIGNIFICANCE AND CLASSICAL LANGUAGES', 'g'),
  bx('pk', '<b>Statutory soul:</b> the Official Languages Act moved India from “Hindi-only” to a <b>permanent bilingual</b> reality. No national language = deliberate “Status Quo”. Language is a <b>“fault line”</b>; <b>Three-Language Formula</b> (Regional, Hindi, English) bridges it but faces implementation problems.'),
